  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to peaceful transition period and elections in South Sudan.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support a peaceful transition and post-conflict recovery in South Sudan by empowering the SSSCBC structure, including Justice and Peace coordinators and bishops, in their advocacy for the constitutional review process. The Church believes that a strong constitutional framework will help establish governance systems and structures that truly reflect the will of the people, ensuring the delivery of public and social services that meet citizens&apos; needs. The project is grounded in the belief that the National Conference can effectively promote a peaceful transition only if it is equipped with the necessary skills and knowledge.





 support the National Conference of Catholic Bishops of South Sudan and the South Sudan Council of Churches (SSCC)empower Church leaders, women, youth and PWDs to engage and contribute to peaceful electoral process toward conclusion of the transition agenda in South Sudan. It is anticipated that the identified activities including deepening understanding of the context through landscape analysis, capacity building, exchange and learning sessions, will lead to citizens capable of resisting violence and opting for dialogue and peaceful resolution of conflicts.</narrative>
  </description>
